# DTF tier manifest: chunked-upload-format-finalize
#   artifact-keeper#1846: a chunked upload (/api/v1/uploads) into a Maven,
#   npm, PyPI or RPM repository is indexed by the format exactly as a single
#   upload through the format's own route is.
#   Profile-set: storage.s3 (MinIO), so the Maven POM and npm tarball are
#   parsed from the staged chunks on the backend and the wheel and RPM from a
#   local assembly, the two completion paths.
#
# THE GAP
#   PUT /api/v1/uploads/{id}/complete committed a generic artifacts row (named
#   after the file, no format metadata) for every format except Incus and
#   Debian (#4413). maven-metadata.xml is generated from rows carrying a
#   `maven` metadata document, the npm packument and the PyPI simple index
#   look rows up by package name, so a chunked jar, tarball or wheel never
#   appeared in its index; an RPM showed in primary.xml (the completion parsed
#   its header) but its row and catalog entry were named after the file.
#
# Gates:
#   (CONTROL, both images) the same artifacts uploaded through each format's
#   own route (Maven PUT, npm publish, twine-style POST, RPM PUT) into a
#   second repository of each format appear in that repository's index.
#   (FIX) the chunked jar + POM appear in maven-metadata.xml; the chunked npm
#   tarball appears in the packument with its package.json dependencies; the
#   chunked wheel appears in /simple/<project>/ with data-requires-python; the
#   chunked RPM's row and catalog entry carry its NEVRA name and
#   version-release (and it is in primary.xml); a tarball whose package.json
#   names another package is refused with 400 and stores nothing;
#   `Prefer: respond-async` answers 202 and polls to completed.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: back-to-back API calls.
#
# Red: ak-backend:1.11.5. Green: ak-backend:lane-w3a.
PROFILES="storage.s3"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
